title: Epilogue
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
when: $outcome == "true_around"
---
The true border goes into the charter, and the new road goes around the mill, the long way, the old way. #line:Epilogue.4b47e708_0100
Bram's wheel turns all summer. The steward's carts curse the corner, and take it anyway. #line:Epilogue.4b47e708_0200
<<detour Accounts>>
===

title: Epilogue
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
when: $outcome == "true_through"
---
The true border goes into the charter. But the road goes straight, as the steward wanted, and the mill is in its way. #line:Epilogue.52c1d3fb_0100
Bram grinds his last sack at midsummer and gives the millstones to the chapel. #line:Epilogue.52c1d3fb_0200
<<detour Accounts>>
===

title: Epilogue
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
when: $outcome == "forged"
---
The steward's border goes into the charter. The abbey loses its meadows, and nobody can say quite why. #line:Epilogue.07a2f9a7_0100
<<if $offer == Offer.Accepted>>
    You leave the valley with forty crowns and a map you will never show anyone. #line:Epilogue.07a2f9a7_0200
<<else>>
    Corvin bows to you as he passes. It is not a friendly bow. #line:Epilogue.07a2f9a7_0300
<<endif>>
<<detour Accounts>>
===

title: Epilogue
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
when: $outcome == "exposed"
---
By evening the steward is two valleys away, and the true border is in the charter. #line:Epilogue.ce4a3029_0100
The Countess asks you to stay on as the valley's cartographer. The abbey sends a cheese. #line:Epilogue.ce4a3029_0200
<<detour Accounts>>
===

title: Epilogue
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
when: $outcome == "walked"
---
The border follows the path the village walks, stone to stone. Nobody is pleased, and nobody fights. #line:Epilogue.9fec7611_0100
Every spring after, the children of Ashcombe and the novices of the abbey walk it together, and argue all the way. #line:Epilogue.9fec7611_0200
<<detour Accounts>>
===

title: Epilogue
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
when: $outcome == "failed"
---
The hearing breaks up without a border. The valley goes home and keeps the quarrel for another generation. #line:Epilogue.b9369c5a_0100
You fold the map with its holes and take the road over the hill. #line:Epilogue.b9369c5a_0200
<<detour Accounts>>
===

title: Accounts
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: Accounts
---
// What is left of every quest, whatever the ending. Jory's line is a line group: one of the lines that fit.
<<if $quest_border == QuestState.Active>>
    <<set $quest_border to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed border>>
<<endif>>
=> Jory dances at the fair on his crutch, and his mother doesn't let go of his sleeve all day. <<if $jory_found>> #line:Accounts_0100
=> Jory buys the first cider of the fair for the whole camp, and the camp drinks it twice. <<if $jory_found>> #line:Accounts_0200
=> Under the hill, Gudrun's miners are still digging for Jory. They say they hear him singing. <<if not $jory_found>> #line:Accounts_0300
=> Nobody under the hill says Jory's name aloud, in case the hill hears. <<if not $jory_found>> #line:Accounts_0400
<<if $quest_recipe == QuestState.Succeeded>>
    Hedda's fair cake, from her mother's recipe, is gone before noon. #line:Accounts_0500
<<endif>>
<<if $quest_lio_map == QuestState.Succeeded>>
    Lio's first map hangs behind Hedda's bar, framed, with the old line in red. #line:Accounts_0600
<<endif>>
<<if $feast_served>>
    The cook of Varne castle still talks about the feast. #line:Accounts_0700
<<endif>>
<<if $pell_trust >= 1>>
    Pell's cart goes over the hill with your story painted on its side. #line:Accounts_0800
<<endif>>
<<if $echo_answered>>
    The echo of the deep level never asks another riddle. #line:Accounts_0900
<<endif>>
<<ending {$outcome}>>
===
